Bug: after a backend restart, a job’s “Last run” summary (status + timestamp on the card) shows “never run” even when its History panel correctly lists completed past runs. Root cause: “Last run” is read from in-memory-only state that resets on restart, while History correctly reads from persisted on-disk run records (meta.json) — two sources of truth for the same fact, only one of which survives a restart.
Fix: for any job with history enabled (history_limit > 0), stop tracking “Last run” as separate in-memory state entirely. Instead, derive it directly from the same persisted history data already used for the History list — simply the most recent entry — so there’s exactly one source of truth for both, and no special “re-hydrate on startup” step is needed since it’s computed fresh each time rather than cached. For jobs with history disabled (history_limit = 0), it’s correct and expected for “Last run” to reset after a restart, since nothing is persisted for those by design — leave that case unchanged.
